+- **Cleared from below:** built an exhaustive taxonomy of regime change unaided, external versus internal. Drew the distinction between a change of regime and a change of regime-form, which is the distinction the whole question turns on. When told his selection argument was unfalsifiable, converted it into a differential prediction — elements coupled to the circumstances persist, uncoupled elements drift, with language as the observed case.
+- **Blocked from above:** every concrete fact in the conversation came from the interviewer. He volunteered one piece of chronology, placing the Ptolemies after Rome rather than before, and had it backwards. The framework he built would have been identical for the Indus Valley or Han China. This is the counterfeit band the ladder warns about — general reasoning strong enough to impersonate knowledge of a subject — and the tell is that the theory arrived before any facts did.
