+Equilibrium, catalysis and reaction coupling were all covered in this session and are no longer frontier. What remains open is reaction mechanisms and rate laws — what the elementary steps actually are, and why rate does not follow stoichiometry. Then electrochemistry, reactions driven by, and driving, electron flow. Then acid-base chemistry as a worked case of equilibrium he now has the tools for.
